<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ismail Adil Shah</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1534</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ismail <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adil-shah">Adil Shah</a> was the second Adil Shahi sultan of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bijapur">Bijapur</a>, succeeding his father <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yusuf-adil-shah">Yusuf Adil Shah</a> in 1510 and ruling until 1534. Like his father he favoured Shia <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a> and Persian immigrants at court. His reign was dominated by conflict with Vijayanagara, whose king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/krishnadevaraya">Krishnadevaraya</a> defeated him at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/raichur">Raichur</a> in 1520, and with the rival <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deccan-sultanates">Deccan sultanates</a>.</p></div>
